{
	"version": 5,
	"rows": [
		{
			"id": "ebL_mNV-XH_qeEHYm",
			"description": "Slugga",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The slugga is the Ork sidearm: a stamped, riveted, big-bore auto-pistol every Boy carries alongside his choppa. Codex: Orks background and Deathwatch's Mark of the Xenos both describe it as crude but powerful - an oversized handgun firing a round more akin to a rifle cartridge than a pistol round - and it is a constant visual in Black Library Ork fiction as the \"boom\" half of \"choppa and shoota\" Ork close-combat doctrine.\n\nDesign: 7d pi+ (avg 24.5). Flak is DR 30, and at the old 5d a big-bore Ork sidearm could never penetrate it, which does not fit a weapon that fires a rifle- sized round from a pistol frame. At 7d, exact dice distribution gives 9.4% through flak (a real but unreliable threat) and 0% against carapace or better, keeping the slugga clearly below the Shoota (57.6% through flak). The same 7d as the Imperial autogun, but its pi+ round is a much fatter bullet, so it wounds harder than the autogun's plain pi. TL 7 sits level with the autogun (framework TL table, solid-projectile tech 7-8); Ork crudeness is carried by Malf, not by a lower TL. Handling: 5 lb; min ST 9 (raw formula sqrt(10x5)=7.1, bumped for a punishing pistol-frame round, the same logic the Imperium Bolt Pistol's ST bump uses), trivial for a Boy (ST 22) but a serious handful for an unaugmented human. Shots 14(3) and Rcl 3 follow from the heavy cartridge. Bulk -2 and Acc 1 follow the framework's low-Acc Ork bracket. Malf 14. Ork weapons never explode on a critical failure; they jam instead.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Orks"
			],
