		{
			"id": "es37N0-yfVLGYJCQ4",
			"description": "Rokkit Pistol",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A rarer, one-handed rokkit tube favoured by Kommando Nobz and Freebooter captains who want an anti-armour punch without giving up a choppa or power klaw in the other hand; smaller and shorter-ranged than the shoulder-fired rokkit launcha, and correspondingly less common in background art, but a recurring \"big pistol\" silhouette in Ork Kommando and Freebooter illustrations.\n\nDesign: Scaled down one size class from the rokkit launcha anchor (6dx4(3) cr ex) the same way this project scales a pistol from its parent rifle family elsewhere: two dice down, same mechanism and armour divisor, giving 4dx4(3) cr ex (avg 56). Exact dice distribution: penetrates carapace (DR 70, eff. 23.3) 99.6% of the time and Astartes power armour (DR 100, eff. 33.3) 94.6% - still a real Marine-killer at short range - but drops off hard against a Terminator (DR 200, eff. 66.7) to 23.9%, and against vehicles clears AV10/AV11 (66.4%) but fails AV12 upward (23.9%/0.4%/0%) - a real but weaker cousin of the full rokkit launcha, matching its rarer, smaller-warhead depiction. Handling: 10 lb loaded (a stubby tube and single warhead, no shoulder stock); min ST 12 (heavier than a slugga for the rocket motor and blast shield, light work for a Nob at ST 34); RoF 1 and Shots 1(6) - a single-shot tube that needs a fresh rocket socketed in by hand, slower even than the full launcha's reload since there's no shoulder brace to steady the reload. Bulk -4 (bulkier than any pistol, still one-handable) and Rcl 1 (the rocket motor, not the launch charge, does the accelerating). Acc 0, per the framework's Ork Acc bracket, worse even than the full launcha for the shorter sighting length. Malf 14, standard Ork gear.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Orks"
			],
