		{
			"id": "etYvBgFrlqmmhrBvr",
			"description": "Shoota",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The shoota is the Ork long arm: a heavy, crudely-stamped automatic weapon built to spray \"dakka\" rather than aim, consistently described across Codex: Orks and Deathwatch's Mark of the Xenos as more effective in volume than in precision, and a constant background weapon in every piece of Ork art and Black Library Ork fiction from the Waaagh!-era novels onward. Ork tech-lore holds that a shoota fires better the louder its owner shouts at it - a detail played for both humour and genuine menace in the fiction, since the effect (whatever its cause) is real in-universe.\n\nDesign: 9d pi+ (avg 31.5). The framework calls shootas heavy slugs, and with flak at DR 30 a 7d shoota would be no better than the Imperium autogun (9.4% through flak), which cannot produce the Guard lines mown down by Ork dakka. Exact dice distribution at 9d: 57.6% through flak, 0% against carapace or better, and 0% against every vehicle AV on the table (AV10-14), so it threatens unarmoured and flak-class targets only. The family escalates shoota < kustom shoota/snazzgun < big shoota < deffgun. TL 7, level with the autogun it outguns. Handling: 20 lb; min ST 16 (raw formula sqrt(10x20)=14.1, bumped for the harder-kicking action), easy for a Boy (ST 28). Shots 24(5); Rcl 4 matches the framework's heavy-stubber bracket of 3-4. RoF 10 and Bulk -5 are the size class; Acc 1 is the dakka-not-precision identity. Malf 14 per the framework's Ork-gear rule (15 within a WAAAGH!, see WAAAGH! Gestalt).",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Orks"
			],
			"tech_level": "7",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "220",
			"base_weight": "20 lb",
