		{
			"id": "ezYTcqp8eoZ_y4UcM",
			"description": "Kustom Shoota",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Mekboy-tuned shoota, its receiver welded over with extra plating, a bigger ammo hopper and (usually) at least one more barrel than it needs: Ork background material is consistent that a Mek's \"kustom\" work makes a weapon hit harder at the direct cost of reliability, since the Mek's improvements are guided by instinct and belief rather than any real engineering discipline.\n\nDesign: 10d pi+ (avg 35), one die over the plain Shoota: a Mek's overbuilt action hits a step harder at the cost of reliability. Exact dice distribution: 79.5% through flak (DR 30) against the plain Shoota's 57.6%, still 0% against carapace or better. A harder-hitting Shoota, not a different class of weapon. TL 7 as the Shoota. Handling: 22 lb (extra plating and a bigger drum over the plain Shoota's 20 lb); min ST 17 (raw formula sqrt(10x22)=14.8, bumped for the heavier housing, one above the plain Shoota's 16); Rcl 4. RoF 12 (the reworked action cycles faster than stock) and Bulk -5 are unchanged in class. Shots 24(5) as the plain Shoota. Malf 13, the framework's kustom-job rating.",
