		{
			"id": "e2eHKN9F0Qy0aQRLd",
			"description": "Big Shoota",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A heavy-stubber-class weapon carried two-handed by a big Ork rather than tripod-mounted by a human crew, common as a Nob's personal weapon, a trukk or battlewagon pintle gun, and standard wargear for the biggest Boyz in a mob. Codex: Orks background places it squarely in the heavy-stubber weight class, and it is a recurring silhouette on Ork vehicle art throughout the game's background material.\n\nDesign: 13d pi+ (avg 45.5). The framework calls the big shoota heavy-stubber class and up. With flak at DR 30 and the plain Shoota at 57.6%, a big shoota needs real daylight above its little brother: exact dice distribution gives 99.3% through flak, essentially 0% through carapace (0.0006%) and 0% against every vehicle AV (AV10-14), so it still cannot hurt power armour or a vehicle, in line with the Imperium Heavy Stubber's reputation. TL 7 (crew-served class, framework TL table 6-8). Handling: 45 lb, a true heavy machine gun; min ST 24 (raw formula sqrt(10x45)=21.2, bumped for the heavy-calibre recoil), a real load even for a Boy's ST 28 and easy for a Nob (ST 34). At 45 lb and carried two-handed by one Ork it is a man-portable light machine gun, so it uses Guns (Light Machine Gun), as the Aeldari equivalent does. Shots 50(6); Rcl 4, the top of the framework's 3-4 heavy-stubber bracket. RoF 15, Bulk -7 and Acc 1 keep the dakka-not-precision identity. Malf 14 (15 within a WAAAGH!).",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Orks"
			],
