		{
			"id": "ej14I_Iz6iIOpp4Zr",
			"description": "Twin Big Shoota",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Two big shootas bolted to a shared frame and fired together, most often seen as a Deff Dread or battlewagon weapon mount but occasionally wielded by an especially large Ork; Codex: Orks background treats twin-linking as the standard Ork answer to \"the first gun wasn't enough dakka.\"\n\nDesign: Two Big Shootas on a shared frame, so 13d pi+ per hit as the single gun (99.3% through flak, negligible against carapace or better, 0% against every vehicle AV). TL 7. RoF 15x2 records the doubled volume of fire by the standard GURPS convention for linked weapons (the Imperium Storm Bolter uses it too). At 85 lb it is a mounted weapon, so it uses Gunner (Machine Gun) like the Deffgun. Handling: 85 lb, roughly double the single gun for the shared mount and doubled feed; min ST 26 (within a Nob's ST 34 and a strain even for a Boy's 28, so a very big Ork or a vehicle mount); Rcl 4 as the single gun. Shots 100(8), not simply double the single gun's 50, since a shared twin feed is more cramped. Bulk -8, one step worse than the single gun for the doubled frame. Malf 14 per barrel; rolling per barrel is a GM option.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Orks"
			],
			"tech_level": "7",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "1500",
			"base_weight": "85 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "WTEzMRI-l9VC410c4",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "pi+",
						"base": "13d"
					},
					"accuracy": "1",
					"range": "200/600",
					"rate_of_fire": "15x2",
					"shots": "100(8)",
					"bulk": "-8",
					"recoil": "4",
					"strength": "26",
					"usage": "Dakka (both barrels)",
					"usage_notes": "Malf 14 per barrel (roll separately if a GM wants one barrel to jam and not the other). Jams rather than explodes on a critical failure, as the Slugga.",
					"defaults": [
