		{
			"id": "e40y0iS0EBpzH_iF5",
			"description": "Deffgun",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A heavy support gun above the Big Shoota's weight class, mounted on Gunwagons, Deff Dreads and Big Meks' own heavy-support loadouts; background material (Codex: Orks, Forge World's Ork background) treats it as the Ork parallel to a human heavy machine gun proper - bigger, slower-cycling and harder-hitting than a shoota-family weapon, without crossing into rokkit or zzap-gun anti-armour territory.\n\nDesign: 15d pi+ (avg 52.5), one clear step above the Big Shoota on the same pi+ solid-slug family. Exact dice distribution: 100% (99.97%) through flak (DR 30) and a small genuine crack in carapace (DR 70) at 0.3%, against the Big Shoota's negligible 0.0006%. Still 0% against every vehicle AV (AV10-14), so it is an infantry-killer, the role rokkits and the Zzap Gun fill for armour. TL 7. Handling: 75 lb; the raw ST formula gives sqrt(10x75)=27.4, but it is always pintle- or arm-mounted, so it takes the M suffix at ST 28 (the mount bears the weight). RoF 10, below the Big Shoota's 15, for the heavier round with a slower cycle. Shots 60(8); Bulk -8; Rcl 4. Acc 1, the Ork-gear figure. Malf 14 (15 within a WAAAGH!).",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Orks"
			],
			"tech_level": "7",
			"legality_class": "0",
