		{
			"id": "eRlivHuG8WK0G80cT",
			"description": "Rokkit Launcha",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Ork anti-armour weapon of choice: a crude, shoulder-fired rocket tube that Codex: Orks and Deathwatch's Mark of the Xenos both describe as good enough to crack open light and medium Imperial armour despite (or because of) its total lack of finesse - fiction across the Ork range consistently shows rokkits cracking Chimeras, Sentinels and Rhinos while struggling against a main battle tank's frontal glacis.\n\nDesign: Matches the framework's Ork anchor (\"Rokkit launcha | Anti-armour, about 6dx4(3) cr ex, Acc 0-1, Malf 14\"). Exact dice distribution against the personal-armour and vehicle-AV tables: avg 84, penetrating every personal armour up to and including Astartes power armour (100%, 100%, 100%, 99.9%) and even a Terminator 85.5% of the time. Against the vehicle table it clears AV10-11 (99.9%/98.0%) reliably, AV12 (85.5%) usually, but falls to 36.3% at AV13 and 2.0% at AV14: it reliably wrecks a Chimera, Rhino or Sentinel, sometimes cracks a Predator-weight hull and rarely beats a Leman Russ or Land Raider outright. A shoulder-fired rocket tube, so it uses Gunner (Rockets) like the Imperium and Aeldari rocket launchers. TL 7, level with the Imperium missile launcher (7-8). Handling: 20 lb loaded, min ST 14 (raw formula sqrt(10x20)=14.1, unmodified). RoF 1 and Shots 1(6): single-shot and hand-loaded, slower than the Imperium Missile Launcher's 1(4) for the cruder loading. Bulk -7 and Rcl 1 (the rocket motor ignites clear of the tube) suit a shoulder-fired tube. Acc 1, the top of the anchor's 0-1 bracket. Malf 14.",
