		{
			"id": "eZP1HBOpPtZwEQsRd",
			"description": "Kustom Mega-Blasta",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Big Mek's own signature weapon: a hand-built, unstable energy gun that Codex: Orks background repeatedly describes in the same breath as \"as likely to explode as to work,\" yet devastating when it doesn't. Widely depicted in Codex art and Ork fiction (no single canonical pattern) as a one-of-a-kind weapon specific to the Mek who built it, rather than a mass-produced pattern.\n\nDesign: No framework anchor covers this item by name, so it is built as an Ork answer to the Imperium's plasma family (TL 10 as an Ork energy weapon, a step below the Imperium's TL 11 plasma) - the closest real-world analogue to \"unstable energy weapon that occasionally kills its own user\" this project already has a design pattern for (see the Plasma Gun's supercharged-mode Malf 14 rule) - but pushed further into Ork unreliability territory. Checked by exact dice distribution: 6dx4(2) burn ex averages 84 and penetrates Astartes power armour (DR 100, eff. 50) 98.0% of the time and even a Terminator (DR 200, eff. 100) 14.5% of the time, putting it in the same tier as the Imperium Plasma Gun against Astartes plate while falling well short of a lascannon against the heaviest armour on the table - a Big Mek's toy is a real Marine-killer, not a tank-killer. Against vehicles it clears AV10 (98.0%) and usually AV11 (72.1%) but fails AV12 upward. Handling: 30 lb, a genuinely heavy hand weapon reflecting a bulky, improvised containment vessel; min ST 22 (a Boy's own strength, per the framework's \"built for Ork hands\" rule, though in practice usually a Big Mek or a burly Boy carries it). RoF 1 and Shots 4(10): a slow, unstable capacitor that must fully recharge between shots and holds only a handful of charges before needing a lengthy re-arm. Bulk -6 and Rcl 2 fit a heavy two-handed energy weapon. Acc 1, the standard Ork figure - a Mek's genius goes into raw power, never sights. Malf 13 (kustom job) with the explicit misfire-injury note, since \"as likely to explode as to work\" is exactly the fiction's own description and deserves a real mechanical consequence, not just a jam.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Orks"
			],
			"tech_level": "10",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "4000",
			"base_weight": "30 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "WGVqz7FyKGqA_J164",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "burn ex",
						"base": "6dx4",
						"armor_divisor": 2
					},
					"accuracy": "1",
					"range": "100/300",
					"rate_of_fire": "1",
					"shots": "4(10)",
					"bulk": "-6",
					"recoil": "2",
					"strength": "22",
					"usage": "Standard",
					"usage_notes": "Malf 13 (kustom job). On a malfunction the containment coil fails catastrophically: the wielder immediately takes 3d(5) burn ex, and the weapon is disabled until a Mek repairs it (Mechanic (Ork Tech) roll, GM's discretion on time and difficulty).",
					"defaults": [
						{
