		{
			"id": "eoEcN6VM2fGyBbpGR",
			"description": "Burna",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Originally a Mekboy's cutting and welding tool, the burna is pressed into service as a crude flamethrower by any Ork strong enough to carry one - background material (Codex: Orks) is explicit that its two uses are the same piece of kit, not two separate items, and Ork fiction shows Burna Boyz using the torch head to carve through both bulkheads and enemies interchangeably.\n\nDesign: The flame-jet mode reuses the Imperium Flamer's own damage and follow-up profile unchanged (3d burn / 1d burn ignoring DR - see the Imperium flame-weapon file), since nothing in Ork background suggests its raw output differs from a human-portable flamer's promethium jet, only its build quality and reliability. The cutting-torch mode is built as a short-range, DR-piercing melee tool rather than a weapon with an anchor: thr+1d(2) burn represents a focused cutting flame at point-blank range, armour divisor (2) for the way a torch head concentrates heat through a seam rather than across a broad hit, cannot parry since the wielder is holding a lit torch, not a blade. Handling: 15 lb loaded, a heavy hand tool with an integral fuel tank; min ST 12 for the ranged mode (a Boy manages it without difficulty). Range 4, shorter than the Imperium flamer's, for a smaller, cruder nozzle; Shots 1(4), one fuel charge per burst with a slow, jury-rigged reload. Bulk -5 fits a bulky two-part device. Malf 13, the kustom-job rating, since every burna is a Mek's individual, hand-modified tool rather than a mass-produced pattern.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Orks"
			],
