		{
			"id": "e1S1oNfSQf5oLs2QY",
			"description": "Skorcha",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A heavier, vehicle-scale burna carried by especially big Orks or mounted as a Battlewagon and Deff Dread weapon; Codex: Orks background places it a clear step above the hand-held burna in both reach and fuel capacity, used for clearing entrenched infantry ahead of an Ork advance rather than as a Mek's personal tool.\n\nDesign: One size class up from the Burna's flame-jet mode (no cutting-torch mode; this is a dedicated infantry-clearing weapon, not a Mek's multitool): 5d burn (avg 17.5) and a proportionally bigger follow-up (1d+1 against the Burna's 1d). Like every flame weapon in this project it has no armour divisor and is not checked against DR-heavy targets; its role is unarmoured and lightly armoured infantry, matching the lore's clearing of entrenched infantry. Handling: 35 lb, a heavy two-handed or mounted weapon with a much bigger fuel tank than the Burna's; min ST 18 (raw formula sqrt(10x35)=18.7, essentially unmodified), within a Boy's ST 28 and easy for a Nob. Range 7, longer than the Burna's 4, for a proper nozzle rather than a cutting-torch head. Shots 1(6), a bigger tank than the Burna's with a slower refill. Bulk -6 fits its size. Malf 14, plain Ork-issue rather than a Mek's individual kustom job, since Skorchas are built to a more consistent (if still crude) pattern for squad-level issue.",
