		{
			"id": "eJsA5A8YWniOtBvuR",
			"description": "Grot Blasta",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A cut-down, simplified slugga built to a Gretchin's much smaller hands and much smaller strength; Codex: Orks background and Ork army art consistently show armed Grots carrying an obviously scaled-down, even-more-slapdash version of Ork small arms rather than a full-sized weapon they couldn't hope to lift or aim.\n\nDesign: Not simply scaled down from the Slugga: even a 7d pi+ Slugga in a Gretchin's hands would be a real threat to flak, which contradicts every depiction of an armed Grot as expendable support fire rather than a combat threat in its own right. Built instead for a Gretchin's own frame (ST 8 per the framework's Ork table) from a smaller, lighter cartridge a Grot can actually cycle: 2d+1 pi (avg 8), without the pi+ wounding bonus the bigger Ork small arms share. Exact dice distribution: 0% against flak (DR 30) or better, so a threat only to unarmoured targets; it is the one deliberately weak entry in this file, a weak pistol rather than a miniature Slugga. TL 7 as the rest of the Ork small-arms family. Handling: 3 lb, a genuinely small pistol; min ST 5 (raw formula sqrt(10x3)=5.5, rounded down to sit within a Grot's ST 8). RoF 3, Shots 10(4), Bulk -2 and Rcl 2 are scaled-down pistol figures. Acc 0, since a Grot-built copy has worse sights than even the shoota family's already-low Acc. Malf 14: Ork tech does not get more reliable just because a Grot is holding it.",
