		{
			"id": "eD2NdChjjknjsm-kk",
			"description": "Kombi-Weapon, Shoota/Rokkit",
			"local_notes": "Lore: An Ork answer to the Imperium's combi-weapons: a shoota with a single rokkit tube welded underneath or alongside the barrel, letting a Nob or Mek carry an anti-armour answer without giving up a rifle's worth of dakka; Ork army art and Codex background both show these improvised combination weapons as a recurring, if unofficial, field modification.\n\nDesign: The shoota barrel follows the plain Shoota's profile (9d pi+, avg 31.5; 57.6% through flak, 0% against carapace or better), with a magazine cut to 16 rounds to make room for the rokkit tube's mounting hardware. The rokkit barrel reuses the Rokkit Launcha's damage line (6dx4(3) cr ex) for a single shot, and uses Gunner (Rockets) as the launcha does; welding a second tube onto a shoota does not change the warhead inside it. Handling: both barrels share one stock, so both usage lines carry the same ST and Bulk. 40 lb loaded (the plain Shoota's 20 lb housing plus the launcha's 20 lb tube, trimmed for a shared stock); min ST 18 (above the plain Shoota's 16 for the added mass and unbalancing tube), well within a Boy's or Nob's strength; Rcl 4 as the plain Shoota. RoF is per mechanism: 10 for the shoota barrel, 1 for the hand-loaded rokkit. Bulk -6, one step worse than the plain Shoota's -5, for the awkward extra tube. Malf 14 on both barrels: a field-welded combination, not a Mek's kustom job.",
