		{
			"id": "eSdMN9ubhWBcIILlN",
			"description": "Kombi-Weapon, Shoota/Burna",
			"local_notes": "Lore: As the Shoota/Rokkit above, with a cut-down burna nozzle and fuel tank welded on in place of the rokkit tube, favoured where a mob expects entrenched infantry rather than armour; the same field-modification tradition Ork background attaches to every kombi pattern.\n\nDesign: The shoota barrel follows the plain Shoota's profile (9d pi+), magazine trimmed to 16 as on the Shoota/Rokkit. The burna barrel reuses the standalone Burna's flame-jet damage (3d burn, with the same DR-ignoring 1d burn follow-up on an ignited target) for a single fuel charge. Handling: 36 lb, lighter than the Shoota/Rokkit's 40 lb for a fuel tank in place of a rocket tube; min ST 18, Bulk -6 and Rcl 4 as the Shoota/Rokkit, since both kombi patterns share the same shoota-plus-auxiliary-tube construction. Malf is per barrel: the shoota half is plain Ork-issue 14, the burna half keeps the standalone Burna's kustom rating of 13, since the flame nozzle is still an individual Mek's hand-fitted work.",
